tllama (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release:
    - Persist scoped REPL input history and add explicit conversation saves.
    - Make /api/ps compact by default with opt-in detailed diagnostics.
    - Forward native device enumeration through tllamad --list-devices.
    - Add optional client terminal notifications, disabled by default.
  * Install the commented client configuration example as
    /etc/tllama/client.toml in the application package, independent of
    tllama-doc. Preserve local configuration edits through dpkg conffiles.

 -- NemaChybu team APT archive <maintainers@nemachybu.cz>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:47:54 +0100

tllama (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release:
    - Add layered client TOML configuration and display preferences.
    - Default human-readable sizes to binary units, with decimal units optional.
    - Expose native fit policy and memory margin configuration.
    - Validate metadata and digest caches against cache-file timestamps.
  * Split guides and configuration examples into the independent tllama-doc
    package; suggest it from the application package.
  * Keep the client, daemon, systemd service, server configuration and man
    pages in tllama, together with the operational Debian README.
  * Retain documentation paths under /usr/share/doc/tllama and declare
    Breaks/Replaces for files moved from pre-1.1.0 application packages.
  * Install the upstream changelog through debhelper, preserving its filename
    link, and include the documentation index and configuration examples.

 -- NemaChybu team APT archive <maintainers@nemachybu.cz>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:11:14 +0100

